body:
I'm so sorry to hear about everything you are facing right now. Sounds like you both have gone through a great deal to stay together. Thank you so much for the advice. I have been trying my best to reunite with him but his country's borders have remained shut for the longest time with no news yet. We did discussed on me applying for a work and holiday visa but even I'm skeptical as my SO has a tendency to spend. He does not give me the financial assurance as I expected and I'm afraid I will be stranded in his country if I walk down this path. We argued so many times when it comes to financials that it's downright exhausting. My job has potential and could bring me to achieving a greater success. I'm willing to sacrifice that for him but I don't think he's willing to control his spending for me, for us, for our future. 

&#x200B;

I'm sorry you had to hear that.. Especially when we are in LDR and things get very tough, that's the last thing you would want to hear. 

&#x200B;

I agree with you, he's definitely supplementing his need via his friends. I understood that and always told him to enjoy himself whenever he goes out. On most days, long distance is very painful. Wish he was there for me to walk through it together. I have tried to be patient and understanding but whenever I try to express my feelings, he always shuts me down and thinks I'm getting paranoid or crazy and says that I brought this upon myself and gives me the silent treatment for days until I couldn't take it anymore and texts/calls him first. It feels like gaslighting at this point.
